# SSH daemon configuration — ECDAT demo target H (SPEC.md §7.4).
#
# Not one of the eight targets §14 lists, but §7.4 ships an sshd_config parser
# and a parser with nothing to parse cannot be tested. Kept as a file rather
# than a running sshd: the parser reads declarations, and nothing in the demo
# probes SSH, so a live daemon would add attack surface and prove nothing.
#
# Everything below is a *declaration*, `source_layer: config`. It is what this
# host claims it will negotiate, and no part of the demo verifies it — which is
# the honest position: unlike the TLS hosts, there is no live observation to
# align it against, so §9 must emit no note for any of it.

Port 22
Protocol 2
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_rsa_key
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ecdsa_key

# ECDAT-EXPECT: config-ssh-ciphers
# CBC-mode SSH ciphers and 3DES. CBC in SSH is worse than in TLS — the mode
# interacts with the packet-length field, which is what CVE-2008-5161 exploits.
Ciphers 3des-cbc,aes128-cbc,aes256-cbc,aes128-ctr,aes256-ctr

# ECDAT-EXPECT: config-ssh-kex
# group1 is the 1024-bit MODP group, and both group1 and group14 hash with
# SHA-1. All three are key-exchange primitives, so Mosca applies to them.
KexAlgorithms diffie-hellman-group1-sha1,diffie-hellman-group14-sha1,ecdh-sha2-nistp256

# ECDAT-EXPECT: config-ssh-macs
# MD5 and truncated-SHA-1 MACs, in encrypt-and-MAC order.
MACs hmac-md5,hmac-sha1-96,hmac-sha2-256

# ECDAT-EXPECT: config-ssh-hostkeyalgorithms
# ssh-rsa is RSA with SHA-1. OpenSSH 8.8 disabled it by default; naming it here
# turns it back on.
HostKeyAlgorithms ssh-rsa,ecdsa-sha2-nistp256

PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
